    "created_at": "2025-12-09T07:18:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-09T07:18:26Z",
    "body": "It seems we can enforce the above even better if we have a single \"origin\" field that holds null, a string, or an origin. (There are some challenges with this as we haven't really defined events properly thus far, but I think that's what we should strive for and allow implementations to do at least.)",
