    "created_at": "2025-12-09T08:16:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-09T08:16:28Z",
    "body": "For `MessageEvent` (and `ExtendableMessageEvent`), I think I'm on board with throwing instead of trying to mint an origin from a string. That has pretty good security properties, and seems like a reasonable precaution to remove one footgun developers might otherwise run into.\n\nHolding a union of strings and origins sounds like a fine approach in the spec. (Though I guess I wonder how useful it is to allow strings to be carried around in the first place; we certainly have tests that depend on arbitrary strings, but I hope that's not actually load-bearing in the real world...)",
